1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,652
Three people, one room, and a decision none of them was ready for.

2
00:00:06,102 --> 00:00:16,102
It took them a dozen choices to get here, and every crew can get here: three of them, or one of them alone.

3
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:24,813
Today you build this, and you learn how to be sure of that last part before anyone plays it.

4
00:00:26,013 --> 00:00:28,187
No rooms yet. Three sentences.

5
00:00:28,637 --> 00:00:31,680
The question: why is this ship drifting?

6
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:40,391
The answer, which the party will find in pieces: her crew put themselves to sleep to wait for help.

7
00:00:40,841 --> 00:00:45,624
And the choice: wake them, or go and get a doctor.

8
00:00:46,074 --> 00:00:52,161
If you cannot write the third sentence you have a tour, not a scene.

9
00:00:52,611 --> 00:00:54,350
Now the beat sheet.

10
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,713
It is just how much of everything. Six places.

11
00:00:59,163 --> 00:01:03,511
One reading for each person on my roster, so three.

12
00:01:03,961 --> 00:01:07,004
One reading for a skill. One check.

13
00:01:07,454 --> 00:01:09,193
That is five facts.

14
00:01:09,643 --> 00:01:13,557
The locked door will ask for three. Two endings.

15
00:01:14,007 --> 00:01:17,050
Keep to these numbers the first time.

16
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:22,598
One room in the middle, and everything hangs off it.

17
00:01:23,048 --> 00:01:25,657
Every room has a way back.

18
00:01:26,107 --> 00:01:32,193
And look where the way home is: in the airlock, and nowhere else yet.

19
00:01:32,643 --> 00:01:35,687
In Lecture 2 every room had one.

20
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:40,050
Here is what I found when I measured it.

21
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:49,630
One press of Return to the ship, by anybody, ends the visit for everybody, and the place cannot be entered again.

22
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:57,472
In a ten-minute scene with three people, that is one thumb away from no ending at all.

23
00:01:57,922 --> 00:02:00,096
So home is a walk.

24
00:02:00,546 --> 00:02:06,633
Now I delete my practice rooms, all of them, and type five places. Lint.

25
00:02:07,083 --> 00:02:13,170
Two warnings: my old stories are waiting for signals from rooms I just deleted.

26
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:14,924
Lint is right.

27
00:02:15,374 --> 00:02:18,852
I will clear them in a few minutes.

28
00:02:20,052 --> 00:02:23,530
Before I type a reading, I list them.

29
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:28,763
What the fact is, where it is, who is offered it.

30
00:02:29,213 --> 00:02:33,996
And one more column, the one that matters: is it sure?

31
00:02:34,446 --> 00:02:39,663
A fact is sure when any party at all can get it.

32
00:02:40,113 --> 00:02:47,504
A reading for a job is sure, because when the doctor stays home somebody covers for her.

33
00:02:47,954 --> 00:02:50,998
A reading for a skill is not.

34
00:02:51,448 --> 00:02:53,622
Nobody covers for a skill.

35
00:02:54,072 --> 00:02:58,420
And a fact behind a check takes luck. Three sure.

36
00:02:58,870 --> 00:03:00,174
Remember that number.

37
00:03:00,624 --> 00:03:01,928
Now the readings.

38
00:03:02,378 --> 00:03:04,552
Same shape as Lecture 3.

39
00:03:05,002 --> 00:03:10,220
Two of them also send a signal, and that is for later.

40
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:12,420
One check.

41
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:15,478
Anyone may try the main cell.

42
00:03:15,928 --> 00:03:25,493
It goes where the party is passing through anyway, never in front of an ending, and what it teaches is a spare.

43
00:03:25,943 --> 00:03:29,422
Both rooms lead back to the engine room.

44
00:03:30,622 --> 00:03:33,665
The captain's hatch opens at three facts.

45
00:03:34,115 --> 00:03:37,159
Three, because I have three sure facts.

46
00:03:37,609 --> 00:03:42,826
The number on the door is never more than the sure facts.

47
00:03:43,276 --> 00:03:45,450
The other two are spares.

48
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:54,596
And two lines on the spine, so a party that gets here early is told why the hatch is shut.

49
00:03:55,046 --> 00:04:00,263
Now a warning, because you will want to write more than this.

50
00:04:00,713 --> 00:04:03,757
A condition has three shapes. A job.

51
00:04:04,207 --> 00:04:06,380
A skill and a number.

52
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:08,135
How many facts.

53
00:04:08,585 --> 00:04:09,889
That is all.

54
00:04:10,339 --> 00:04:12,078
There is no and.

55
00:04:12,528 --> 00:04:16,441
You cannot ask for one fact by its name.

56
00:04:16,891 --> 00:04:23,848
Write any of those and lint says clean, and the choice is never offered to anyone.

57
00:04:25,048 --> 00:04:27,222
An ending is three things.

58
00:04:27,672 --> 00:04:34,193
A quest the ship does not have yet: Starts when: revealed, so it is hidden.

59
00:04:34,643 --> 00:04:38,991
A choice that starts it: semicolon, accepts, the quest's key.

60
00:04:39,441 --> 00:04:45,963
You used accepts on an answer in Class 2, and it works the same here.

61
00:04:46,413 --> 00:04:53,804
And a last room, with one line and one way out, and that way out is home.

62
00:04:54,254 --> 00:04:58,167
Do not give a last room a way back.

63
00:04:58,617 --> 00:04:59,922
I tried it.

64
00:05:00,372 --> 00:05:02,546
The party took both endings.

65
00:05:03,746 --> 00:05:12,007
Two stories, the same shape as last time: For, a job, and a signal that person's own reading sends.

66
00:05:12,457 --> 00:05:16,804
Now the ship's quest, and one change from Lecture 5.

67
00:05:17,254 --> 00:05:20,733
Last time it waited for the doctor's story.

68
00:05:21,183 --> 00:05:25,965
So with the doctor at home, it stayed open for good.

69
00:05:26,415 --> 00:05:30,328
This time it waits for the reading's own signal.

70
00:05:30,778 --> 00:05:32,952
The doctor's press finishes both.

71
00:05:33,402 --> 00:05:40,359
And if she is not there, whoever covers for her finishes the ship's quest. Lint. Clean.

72
00:05:41,559 --> 00:05:42,863
Lint is clean.

73
00:05:43,313 --> 00:05:45,487
Lint has checked my spelling.

74
00:05:45,937 --> 00:05:50,720
It has not walked through my rooms, and it never will.

75
00:05:51,170 --> 00:05:52,474
So, five checks.

76
00:05:52,924 --> 00:05:57,272
One: every room has a way out with no if.

77
00:05:57,722 --> 00:05:59,461
Fourteen headings, fourteen ticks.

78
00:05:59,911 --> 00:06:02,954
Two: every room has a way in.

79
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:07,752
Three: the door asks for three, I have three sure.

80
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:16,028
Four, the important one: I cross out everything that needs a skill or luck, and I walk it.

81
00:06:16,478 --> 00:06:19,522
Airlock, spine, three readings, cabin, ending, home.

82
00:06:19,972 --> 00:06:24,320
If the worst crew can do it, every crew can.

83
00:06:24,770 --> 00:06:33,465
Five: each story is finished by its own person's reading, and each last room has one way out. Now watch.

84
00:06:33,915 --> 00:06:37,828
I make the door ask for four. Lint: clean.

85
00:06:38,278 --> 00:06:41,757
But check three: four is more than three.

86
00:06:42,207 --> 00:06:45,685
That scene only opens for a lucky party.

87
00:06:46,135 --> 00:06:48,309
Lint could not tell me.

88
00:06:48,759 --> 00:06:50,063
The pencil could.

89
00:06:51,263 --> 00:06:53,437
Alone first, as the chief.

90
00:06:53,887 --> 00:06:57,800
The doctor's reading comes to me marked as covering.

91
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:59,989
So does the quartermaster's.

92
00:07:00,439 --> 00:07:03,917
Three facts, the hatch, an ending. Sixteen presses.

93
00:07:04,367 --> 00:07:07,846
Now all three, and the watch is running.

94
00:07:08,296 --> 00:07:11,339
Each reading goes to its own person.

95
00:07:11,789 --> 00:07:14,833
Nothing is marked as covering. They choose.

96
00:07:15,283 --> 00:07:22,239
And on the bridge, the ship has a quest it did not have a minute ago.

97
00:07:22,689 --> 00:07:23,993
Stop the watch.

98
00:07:25,193 --> 00:07:26,193
Now yours.

99
00:07:26,643 --> 00:07:33,165
Three sentences, a beat sheet, the places, the facts table, and only then the rooms.

100
00:07:33,615 --> 00:07:35,354
Do the five checks.

101
00:07:35,804 --> 00:07:41,457
Break it three times on purpose and find each one with the pencil.

102
00:07:41,907 --> 00:07:46,254
Then play it, and write down how long it took.

103
00:07:46,704 --> 00:07:53,661
Next time, we open up a long away mission and see how its files fit together.
